At a temperature of $700\text{ K}$ a sample of $\text{HBr}$ is approximately 10% decomposed. Changing the temperature affects both the rate of decomposition of $\text{HBr}$ and the percentage that decomposes.

The Boltzmann distribution for a sample of $\text{HBr}$ at $700\text{ K}$ is shown. $E_a$ represents the activation energy for the reaction.

